within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01F_MonoclonalAntibodiesAndAntibodyDrugConjugates.L01FC02_Isatuximab;
model Isatuximab_Koiwai2021_PD_m_protein_3
  "linear exposure-response sweep — Koiwai_2021 :: M-protein (serum M-protein concentrations)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 21.4,      // [kg/m3; g·L−1 × 1]
    Emax = 0, EC50 = 1,      // unused by a line
    exposure_per_s = 1);
  parameter Real slope = 0.0125   "[mol−1·d−1]";
equation
  response = E0 + slope*exposure;
  // family_inferred: the record's model family is disease_progression; read from the parameters: a slope and no Emax — linear
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1000, Interval = 2),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Isatuximab_Koiwai2021_PD_m_protein_3</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Koiwai K et al., <i>CPT: pharmacometrics &amp; systems pharmacology 10(8):928–940</i> 2021 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/psp4.12666\">doi:10.1002/psp4.12666</a>) — serum M-protein concentrations [g/L] against isatuximab and pomalidomide molar units — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: linear.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       21.4 g·L−1    drug-free response (baseline) (M0, Q324)
  slope =     0.0125 mol−1·d−1 change in response per unit of exposure (KD, Q335)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0 + slope*exposure</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one molar units of isatuximab and pomalidomide per second of simulated time: there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 21.4   (drug-free)</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Koiwai_2021: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Isatuximab_Koiwai2021_PD_m_protein_3;
